safestringlib
------------------------------------------
The Safe String Library is a C Library providing string and memory buffer
routines that protect against buffer overflows.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libsafestring-devel-1.3.0-1bl1
  libsafestring1-1.3.0-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/intel/safestringlib

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/intel/safestringlib/archive/refs/tags/v1.3.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack safestringlib-1.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./safestringlib-1.3.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/safestringlib-1.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/safestringlib-1.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsafestring1-1.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsafestring-devel-1.3.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(safestringlib)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/safestringlib.README
  /usr/share/doc/safestringlib/CHANGELOG.md
  /usr/share/doc/safestringlib/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/safestringlib/LICENSE&COPYING.txt
  /usr/share/doc/safestringlib/README.md

(libsafestring1)
  /usr/bin/cygsafestring-1.dll

(libsafestring-devel)
  /usr/include/safe_lib.h
  /usr/include/safe_lib_errno.h
  /usr/include/safe_mem_lib.h
  /usr/include/safe_str_lib.h
  /usr/include/safe_types.h
  /usr/include/snprintf_s.h
  /usr/lib/cmake/safestring/safestringConfig-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/safestring/safestringConfig.cmake
  /usr/lib/libsafestring.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/safestringlib.pc

